[[File:AK69stand.jpg|175px|thumb|upright|[[AK-69]] held the most number one spots on the chart in 2017, with "Ue wo Muite" (Towards the Top) becoming number one from January 29 to February 5, the record-breaking "Stronger" from June 18 to July 9, "Started from da Bottom" with MC TYSON on October 15, and "I Still Shine" featuring Che'Nelle from October 22 to November 26. "I Still Shine" held the most weeks on the chart with 6 weeks.]]

The '''PYRAMID30 Okaiken''' is a chart that ranks the best-performing singles in [[Okaiken]]. Its data, published by Nikkan Sports & Entertainment magazine, KTK Group and compiled by Okaiken Pyramid Records, is based collectively on each single's weekly physical and digital sales, as well as radio airplay and streaming. PYRAMID30 Okaiken is a subsidiary of Pyramid Records but acts as a separate organization. The weekly charts are updated every Sunday at 11:45 in the morning (UTC +9). The following lists all of the number one singles of the PYRAMID30 Okaiken for 2017.

